# media/windows/hittest-beta1.cmds — what 0.4.1-beta.1 answered: with `legacy-pointer on` the title
# bar's controls are drawn as they were, with nothing keeping a press on them from being a window
# move. Each line passes when the failure is reproduced, so this suite is the proof that
# hittest.cmds would catch it. Windows only.
# Run: pwsh script/capture.ps1 windows/hittest-beta1

pace 0
theme night
glass off
project @REPO@
send hello
wait idle 30000
legacy-pointer on
# Pressed on, each of these started a window move (and the click never came).
hittest toggle-sidebar HTCAPTION
hittest mode-agents HTCAPTION
hittest mode-editor HTCAPTION
hittest pop-out HTCAPTION
hittest toggle-tools HTCAPTION
hittest settle HTCAPTION
# Run and Open are menus that take their press for themselves, so the move never started and they
# worked: the handle, with the press swallowed.
hittest run-actions HTCAPTION:swallowed
hittest open-in HTCAPTION:swallowed
shot hit-beta1
legacy-pointer off
hittest mode-editor HTCLIENT
